# /calendar/ is the public-facing URL for the Performance Calendar page.
# The page itself is physically served from /static/calendar/ (see the
# quartz/quartz/static/calendar/ note in this file's git history for why:
# Quartz's Assets emitter strips the .html extension from any content/*.html
# file, which breaks Netlify's content-type detection -- only quartz/static/
# preserves it). This is a 200 rewrite (not a redirect), so the browser URL
# stays /calendar/ while the response body comes from the real file. The
# calendar's own HTML uses absolute asset paths for exactly this reason.
/calendar   /static/calendar/index.html   200
/calendar/  /static/calendar/index.html   200
